-- title:
--   Atkin–Lehner translate of a configured point exchanges special-fibre components
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a level $M$ divisible by $p$ with $M/p$ nonzero, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the $q$-series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of level-one modular forms. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, i.e. a bundled proper, flat, integral, normal model of $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$ carrying a curve model `Meta` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ together with the isomorphism `eeta` onto its geometric generic fibre, an automorphism $w$ over the base, component maps `comp` and diamonds `dia0` on the special fibre, and a smooth locus. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R_p \to A$ be a ring map inducing the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume `hdia0`: for every unit $e$ of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ and every closed point $P$ of the special-fibre curve `𝔛.Mfib A hA ρ hρ`, transporting $P$ through `efib`, the fibre map of the diamond $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{dia}_0(e)$ and the inverse of `efib` again gives a closed point, whose place is obtained from that of $P$ by the semilinear automorphism attached to `diamondActionModL` over the residue field at level $M/p$ for the image subgroup `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, evaluated at the $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift [`CuspForm.gammaLift (M / p) e`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L36). Let $pb$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ representing $p$, and let `wgen` be a semilinear automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ pinned to $w$ in the sense that whenever two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-sections $y, y'$ of `Meta` satisfy: $y'$ followed by `eeta`, the first projection and $w$ equals $y$ followed by `eeta` and the first projection, then the place of $y'$ is `wgen` applied to the place of $y$. Given $i \in \{0,1\}$, a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-section $y$ of `Meta`, a morphism $u : \operatorname{Spec} A \to X_p(\Gamma_M(M,H))$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \rho$ whose base change along $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the generic point determined by $y$, whose image lies in the smooth locus, together with a section $u_\kappa$ of the residue-field fibre reducing $u$, and a closed point $P$ of the special-fibre curve with $(\mathrm{efib} \text{ followed by } \mathrm{comp}_i)(P)$ the closed point of $u_\kappa$: then there are $y'$ and $u' = u$ followed by $w^{-1}$ with the same three properties (base change of $u'$ is the generic point of $y'$, image in the smooth locus), with place of $y'$ equal to `wgen` applied to the place of $y$, and a section $u'_\kappa$ of the residue-field fibre reducing $u'$ which, composed with the fibre map of $w$, returns $u_\kappa$, and a closed point $P'$ of the special-fibre curve lying on the other component, $(\mathrm{efib} \text{ followed by } \mathrm{comp}_{1-i})(P')$ being the closed point of $u'_\kappa$, whose place is the place of $P$ twisted by the diamond at $pb$ if $i = 0$, and the place of $P$ itself if $i = 1$.
--
--   This is the Atkin–Lehner translation step for the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ at $p \mid M$: $w^{-1}$ carries a point configured on one component of the special fibre to one configured on the other, moving the generic place by `wgen` and the special place by the diamond at the class of $p$ in the exchanged case. It feeds the computation of the Hecke operator $U_p$ and of the degeneracy maps on points of the Néron model of the Jacobian in the `JHNeronObjectAtP` results.
